From 28dbae6cd81282ae2e3192ab5048a04523529a6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:08:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] apu: resample voices, read heap sample data, keep the stream
 continuous

Four fixes found by ear once the monitor stopped wiping the output
(MKSM: noisy, double speed, choppy):

- Sample data from the right store. MmGetPhysicalAddress passes heap
  addresses through unchanged; past XBOX_HEAP_BASE bytes of contiguous
  memory the same number is also a contiguous physical address, and
  mcpx_apu_phys picked the window: sound banks in heap memory played
  texture bytes. mcpx_apu_data_phys (sample reads only) picks heap RAM
  for pages the heap has handed out, cached per 4 KB page per frame.
  RECOMP_APU_DATA_HEAP=0/1 forces window/RAM for A/B.
- Resampling. voice_resample ignored the pitch (libsamplerate stub), so
  content below 48 kHz played too fast: linear interpolation with
  per-voice state carried across frames, reset on VOICE_ON.
- A trapped front end no longer stops the VP (only the method FIFO
  stalls on hardware); the old test, fectl & TRAPPED, also matched
  HALTED. While a started APU has XCNTMODE off or the FE halted, the
  frame thread waits instead of sending silent frames: DirectSound
  toggles XCNTMODE around its voice updates (~30/s during movies).
- throttle() catches up after late wakeups (up to ~53 ms) instead of
  dropping the lost time from the output.

RECOMP_APU_STATS adds stall waits, sample-data reads by store and the
contiguous high-water mark; RECOMP_APU_TRACE_SECTL=1 logs SECTL writes
with the host RIP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
